ed rivers.","","text","",""]]},"N6NZN":{"d":[["Distribution. Japan (Esaki 1931).","","text","",""]]},"N82N4":{"d":[["Distribution: Madagascar, only found in lowland forest streams of the Northwestern part (province Maromandia).","","text","",""]]},"N9MSS":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"N9N2S":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"N9N32":{"d":[["Africa","","text","",""],["Australia","","text","",""],["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""],["North America","","text","",""],["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"NVB4":{"d":[["","PAN-OO","tdwg","native",""],["Panama","","text","native",""]]},"NX3K6":{"d":[["Neotropic","","text","native",""]]},"Q8FY2":{"d":[["Slovenia","48523","mrgid","native",""]]},"QR3Q3":{"d":[["Distribution. New Guinea. Notes. Faust (1898) mentions that the description is based on a single, presumably female specimen. A second specimen arrived at a later date at SMTD and is not part of the type series. Both specimens exhibit some morphological differences and are likely to belong to different, though closely related species.","","text","",""]]},"QYDXT":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","native",""],["Norway","NO","iso","native",""],["Norway","NO","iso","native",""],["Norway","NO","iso","native",""]]},"QYDY3":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","native",""],["Norway","NO","iso","native",""]]},"RXF55":{"d":[["Oceania","","text","",""]]},"SGDH4":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"T8WJM":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"THKS":{"d":[["Ecuador","","text","",""]]},"THL2":{"d":[["Colombia (Caquetá, Huila)","","text","",""]]},"V3CZ4":{"d":[["Distribution. Costa Rica.","","text","",""]]},"V5Q8F":{"d":[["Australia (New South Wales, Victoria [I])","","text","",""]]},"VBXBH":{"d":[["Distribution. Genetically confirmed records of P. h. hyneki sp. et subsp. nov. are presently only known from the type locality in the southeastern DRC. However, there are three iNaturalist records of similar turtles from central Zambia (Kasanka National Park and Mpongwe) that likely represent P. h. hyneki sp. et subsp. nov. as well, even though their collection sites are approximately 600 km away. This is also likely for the two photographic records of “ P. subniger ” with a diffuse plastral pattern in northern Botswana (Khwai [Kwaai] River and Ngamiland) and another photographic record from northeastern Zimbabwe (Fig. 8; Table S 3).","","text","",""]]},"VCBL3":{"d":[["Québec","48408","mrgid","",""]]},"W4KD":{"d":[["St. John (United States Virgin Islands)","20840","mrgid","",""]]},"WCLT":{"d":[["Cocos-Keeling/Christmas Island","21881","mrgid","",""]]},"ZQGH":{"d":[["Madagascar","","text","",""]]}}